  Toeplitz means that `A` has constant diagonals. Hence, `A` can be generated
  with two vectors. One represents the first column of the matrix, and the
  other represents the first row.

  Below is a 4 x 4 example:

  ```
  A = |a b c d|
      |e a b c|
      |f e a b|
      |g f e a|
  ```

